BUILD/TEST BLOCKER (honest, reproduced) — toolchain-version incompatibility
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The only installed Xcode (26.5 / Swift 6.3.2) is NEWER than the repo's pinned
Swift 6.0 toolchain. Under 6.3.2 the PRE-EXISTING baseline does not compile: many
co-located surface files use language patterns the newer frontend rejects. The
build aborts inside files this artifact never touches. Two distinct pre-existing
categories were captured before the build aborts (there are more behind them):

  1) ~80 helper funcs `@ViewBuilder _ content: () -> some View` passed into an
     @escaping panel initializer:
     TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AIAutoNameUnnamedLocations.swift:123:22:
       error: escaping closure captures non-escaping parameter 'content'
     (same shape in ~80 TeslaSync/{shared-surfaces,feature-views,...} helpers)

  2) type-inference timeouts in pre-existing preview bodies:
     TeslaSync/feature-views/RecentDrivesSection.Previews.swift:24:20:
       error: the compiler is unable to type-check this expression in reasonable
       time; try breaking up the expression into distinct sub-expressions

These files are outside this artifact's allowed scope (the prompt limits edits to
the Analytics feature, navigation registration, the string catalog, and this log).
Repairing ~80+ unrelated baseline files across multiple error categories would be a
scope violation and is unbounded. Per the honesty covenant (#1 no red-as-green,
#8 no commit on red, #10 STATUS=<DONE|BLOCKED>) this is reported as BLOCKED, which
matches the prompt's contingency ("If no Xcode runner is available, the gate ->
STATUS=BLOCKED") — here, no toolchain-compatible runner is available.

